10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] ### Issue 1 (Severity 600000): Temporary File Deletion
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] **Problem**: The File-based constructors of TAQWriter were creating temporary files during testing that weren't being cleaned up.
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] **Solution**: Created a factory class (`TAQWriterFactory`) that provides TAQWriter instances using `ByteArrayOutputStream` instead of file-based streams. This approach:
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - Avoids creating temporary files entirely
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - Provides properly initialized TAQWriter instances for testing
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - Eliminates the need for file cleanup logic
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:19:42.128 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] ### Issue 2 (Severity 10): NPE in TAQWriter.close()
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] **Problem**: NullPointerException occurred when calling `close()` because the PrintWriter was trying to write to a BufferedOutputStream with a null underlying stream.
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] **Solution**: The factory method `createTAQWriter()` creates a TAQWriter with a properly initialized `ByteArrayOutputStream`, ensuring that:
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - The entire stream chain (ByteArrayOutputStream → OutputStreamWriter → PrintWriter) is properly initialized
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - The `close()` method can execute without throwing NPE
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] - The factory is annotated with `@InterestingTestFactory` as required
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] ### Issue 3 (Severity 10): NPE in TAQWriter.flush()
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] **Problem**: Similar to Issue 2, NullPointerException occurred when calling `flush()` due to improperly initialized streams.
10:19:42.129 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
